":"text"}]},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/Trees/Forest/init(_:)":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/Trees\/Forest\/init(_:)","title":"init(_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shortest-path forest of a search from any number of sources, with the edges’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directions and the roots dropped: every reached vertex, in the tree’s index order as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Arborescence(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lists them (unreached ones left out), and one edge (parent, child) per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached vertex with a parent, in that order. Edge positions are the forest’s own: edge k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"joins the k-th listed vertex with a parent to its parent; the graph’s edge stays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"tree.parentEdge(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". O(n); the vertices are hashed once, into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forest’s lookup table, unless they are the "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"code":"0..<k","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in order."}],"url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/trees\/forest\/init(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13ShortestPaths0A8PathTreeV","text":"ShortestPathTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":">)"}]},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Trees-Arborescence-Extensions":{"role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafl